|date=September 2, 2011
|author=
|title=Wales 2-1 Montenegro
|work=BBC
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/14660870.stm
|page=
|passage=Defeat 12 months ago away to the same opponents signalled the end of John Toshack's reign as Wales manager, '''ushering in''' first caretaker Brian Flynn and then current boss Gary Speed.}}
# To [[begin]] something with [[preparatory]] material; to [[introduce]].
#: {{ux|en|It '''ushered in''' a whole new era.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021 October 20|author=Dr Joseph Brennan|title=A key part of our diverse railway heritage|journal=RAIL|issue=942|page=56|text=The war-torn first half of the 20th century, together with the railway grouping of 1923, '''ushered in''' further austerity in design.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|work=FT Weekend|date=2023-09-30|title=The wildest job in Silicon Valley|author=Hannah Murphy|section=Life & Arts|page=17|passage=Until recently, journalist inquiries to X's press department received an auto-response of a poop emoji. Yaccarino, attempting to '''usher in''' a friendlier era, greets me warmly.}}

